  "summary": "Acquires event loop references across CapnpProtocol methods and protects the event loop pointer with a mutex. This prevents the IPC event loop from exiting or being destroyed prematurely while methods on other threads are using it.",
  "problem": "In IPC serve mode, only the parent connection holds a reference keeping the event loop alive. Methods on CapnpProtocol called from other threads do not hold references, allowing the loop to exit or be destroyed concurrently if the parent connection drops, leading to race conditions or crashes.",
